<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saudi Arabia sends skyscraper employees home amid Houthi threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1f2e3e701af9a09ce9df2e14673b48cf0ee1684d354dac633f2d711499b522c</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-sends-skyscraper-employees-home-amid-houthi-threats/a-79693225--d3fabe96c473.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-sends-skyscraper-employees-home-amid-houthi-threats/a-79693225?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Riyadh's Kingdom Center tower's management told the people employed there to work from home "until further notice," without giving a reason. This comes as Houthi attacks escalate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Meloni backs police after cost-of-living protests turn violent in Italian cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbf3be89d404debb4d68ace866f4dfbf91710c8a3635896192bd51f08cb91f9a</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/meloni-backs-police-after-cost-of-living-protests-turn-violent-in-italian-cities/a-79692755--6c120f7fa831.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/meloni-backs-police-after-cost-of-living-protests-turn-violent-in-italian-cities/a-79692755?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anger over living costs and low wages has brought Italians onto the streets. A major union has called a general strike for November 20.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine apologizes after a suspected drone crashes in Lithuania, damaging a moving car.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f900129ebd9cb480a764c6663c61860e03f4d74921f145fe3840a829833988e5</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-apologizes-after-a-suspected-drone-crashes-in-lithuania-damaging-a-moving-car/a-79692905--1e1a7cbd41db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-apologizes-after-a-suspected-drone-crashes-in-lithuania-damaging-a-moving-car/a-79692905?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Debris has damaged a moving car in Lithuania, where NATO jets were scrambled. Kyiv says Russian jamming may have diverted drones targeting Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope appears in public for first time since surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e6cacf9acee48ccc1052916e8a5c7cbbbf3857b8fbff60cc0e3c4f68931875</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-appears-in-public-for-first-time-since-surgery/a-79692583--2ad80bce5c46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-appears-in-public-for-first-time-since-surgery/a-79692583?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After undergoing a lung operation, the pope said he will resume his duties gradually. There is no "clinical reason" for his South America trip not to go ahead, his surgeon said.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>France: Young voters blase about Glucksmann's Socialists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69721268dccae48e621a4b012de780ba12ef245e47ba3eec4d2b630890cc33c2</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159--5c98176d41f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Raphael Glucksmann wants to lead France's Socialists to power without working with the left-populist Jean-Luc Melenchon, who is particularly popular with young voters. How can the center-left candidate win them over?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's eight-hour workday under threat?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1793a7a470b7815adacdca42f5b7dd313a5a1b93a11e90421de951b28c39e2b1</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984--28b0ad264d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Would you work 12 hours straight? The CDU/CSU and SPD are locked in a dispute over reforms to the Working Hours Act. Workplace flexibility, collective bargaining agreements and worker protection rules are at stake.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>France reports almost 2,400 arrests after riots, looting and arson during cost-of-living protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df71fb5ed5850001b346d3ea4787505965c817c7f6d14ef59e6294c937e94747</id><updated>2026-10-18T18:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-reports-almost-2-400-arrests-after-riots-looting-and-arson-during-cost-of-living-protests/a-79692322--b9914eaa2c94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="h